# ===========================================================================
#  wam-alert-probe -- fail on purpose, to prove this machine can be heard
# ===========================================================================
#
#      systemctl start wam-alert-probe
#
#  Every watcher on a WAM host says OnFailure=wam-alert@%n.service, and that
#  path has three parts that can each be broken on a new machine: the alert
#  unit, the credentials it sends with, and the network out. A watcher whose
#  alert cannot leave the host is not a watcher; it is a log nobody reads.
#
#  So this unit does nothing except fail, which fires the same OnFailure= as
#  a real fault, and the operator either receives a message or learns that he
#  would not have. It was run on seed3 on 11 September, the day that host
#  joined, and the message arrived.
#
#  WHY IT IS IN THE REPOSITORY NOW
#
#  It was not. It was written straight onto the host as a one-off, and then
#  left in `failed` state for twenty-three hours, where it sat on the
#  operations panel as a red line on an otherwise healthy machine. The
#  founder saw it and asked. A permanent red is worse than no red: it teaches
#  whoever reads the panel to skip that line, and the next red on that line
#  will be a real one, two days before launch or on the night itself.
#
#  ExecStopPost is why it cannot happen again. systemd triggers OnFailure=
#  when the unit fails, and runs ExecStopPost afterwards -- so the alert is
#  already on its way by the time the failed state is cleared. The `-` prefix
#  means that if reset-failed is refused while the unit is still deactivating,
#  the unit simply stays red as it did before, which is no worse than today.
#
#  An undocumented unit on a production host is its own defect. If it is
#  worth running on a machine, it is worth reading in the repository.
# ===========================================================================
[Unit]
Description=Deliberate failure, to prove this machine can be heard
Documentation=https://github.com/wam-coin-official/wam-coin/blob/main/deploy/systemd/wam-alert-probe.service
OnFailure=wam-alert@%n.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/bin/false

# Clear the failed state once the alert has been triggered, so the probe does
# not leave a red line on the panel for the next person to learn to ignore.
ExecStopPost=-/usr/bin/systemctl reset-failed %n
